AB  - Fine-tuning LLMs is therefore essential in their performance polishing towards highly specific tasks. Pre-trained LLMs usually function exceptionally in general natural language processing tasks, whereby their performance drops in specialized domains due to the lack of contextual knowledge and understanding of the respective task. This paper surveys different fine-tuning methods, including instruction tuning, Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA), and quantization techniques. These methods are analyzed regarding their pros and cons, especially in relation to their performance on the model in terms of accuracy, generalization, and computation efficiency. Results indicate that finetuning shows a higher effectiveness, enhancing model adaptability and performance in specialized tasks, including scientific text classification, secure code generation, programming evaluation. The paper concludes with recommendations for advanced finetuning approaches that can enhance the efficiency of LLMs in specialized areas.
