AB  - Large Language Models (LLMs) have garnered significant attention in the field of Artificial Intelligence due to their impressive performance across a wide range of natural language tasks, such as understanding, generation, and manipulation, following the development of transformer-based models, a key innovation in the evolution of LLMs. The research area of LLMs, while still relatively new, is evolving rapidly in various ways, from improving model architecture to improving efficiency and application versatility. This paper provides a comprehensive overview LLMs that address Arabic language processing. It also explores recent advances in Arabic transformer-based models, highlighting their characteristics, contributions, and limitations. We then focus on the applications of LLMs in opinion analysis, specifically how they can be utilized to extract key insights from social media data. Finally, we conclude with open challenges and future research directions. This review is intended as a quick and comprehensive reference for researchers and practitioners to draw insights from extensive summaries of existing works to advance LLM research.
