AB  - This tutorial provides a comprehensive overview of the research landscape of employing Large Language Models (LLMs) to spatial analysis queries. The tutorial categorizes the research in this area along two directions. The first focuses on the underlying spatial data being processed. Spatial data types include traffic data, trajectory data, POI data, and multi-modal data. The second direction focuses on how LLMs are employed to serve spatial queries. This goes from employing LLMs as is, to fine-tuning LLMs, and completely retraining LLM from scratch, to modifying the LLM internals and loss function to better fit such queries. The tutorial concludes by a set of benchmarks and points out to research gaps and future research directions.
ER  - 

