AB  - E-commerce product classification provides convenience to customers in searching for products. Due to the ever-increasing number of categories in e-commerce product classification, the traditional rule-based approach has proved to be extremely inefficient. This paper includes the implementation of various deep learning models such as CNN on the Image Dataset and BERT with zero-shot learning on the Amazon Product Dataset 2023. This paper aims to understand the performance of these models and their limitations with respect to unstructured and unclean product descriptions. From the results, it can be clearly identified that CNN and BERT work extremely well with well-structured data. However, the accuracy of these models decreases significantly when the same models are applied to unclean data. GPT can be identified as a zero-shot learning model that provides the utmost flexibility to generalize the model to various product categories. However, the accuracy of the model decreases significantly. Despite the model being highly accurate in handling unknown classes compared to traditional deep learning models, the model fails to provide consistent accuracy with respect to various product classification datasets.
ER  - 

